      "text": "Let's denote the measure of the angle as \\( x \\) degrees. The measure of its complement is \\( 90 - x \\) degrees. According to the problem, the angle is double the measure of its complement. Therefore, we can write the equation:\n\n\\[ x = 2(90 - x) \\]\n\nSolving for \\( x \\):\n\n\\[ x = 180 - 2x \\]\n\\[ x + 2x = 180 \\]\n\\[ 3x = 180 \\]\n\\[ x = \\frac{180}{3} \\]\n\\[ x = 60 \\]\n\nSo, the degree measure of the angle is 60 degrees.\n\nTo confirm the solution, let's check the complementary angle:\n\n\\[ 90 - 60 = 30 \\]\n\nAnd double that:\n\n\\[ 2 \\times 30 = 60 \\]\n\nIndeed, the angle is double the measure of its complement. Thus, the final answer is:\n\n\\(\\boxed{60}\\)",
